From 6a660221c859229b88107edd86658d0bcbaec5cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: evilcomputer12 <martinrobotika@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 07:53:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/21] xgameruntime: Parse the game identity, visuals, StoreId
 and install directory from MicrosoftGame.config.

ObtainMsaAppId() now also keeps Identity@Name/@Publisher/@Version,
ShellVisuals@DefaultDisplayName/@PublisherDisplayName and <StoreId>, and
records the directory of the config it found as a Windows path (no trailing
backslash) and as a unix path. They are exposed to the C and C++ sources as
the gdk_* globals in private.h; a missing value leaves "" rather than NULL.

gdk_package_identifier is the Windows package full name
"<Name>_<Version>_x64__<publisher id>", the publisher id being the Crockford
base32 form of the first 8 bytes of SHA-256 over the UTF-16LE Publisher
string, as in package family names (a small embedded SHA-256 keeps bcrypt
out of the import list). Balatro gives PlayStack.Balatro_1.0.5.0_x64__3wcqaesafpzfy.

The options != NULL branch of ObtainMsaAppId always failed with
E_GAMERUNTIME_GAMECONFIG_BAD_FORMAT (broken if/else-if chain); it now parses
the inline or file config and falls through like the search path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../GDKComponent/InitInternalGDKC.cpp         | 214 +++++++++++++++++-
 dlls/xgameruntime/private.h                   |  25 ++
 2 files changed, 232 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

